No third-party code is copied. The shapes firmcall writes follow public documentation, as read on 2026-10-02:
- Managed settings, managed-settings.d, the MDM preference domain com.anthropic.claudecode, the HKLM key:
  https://code.claude.com/docs/en/managed-settings
- Permission rule paths (//, ~/, /, relative): https://code.claude.com/docs/en/permissions
- Organisation plugins, strictKnownMarketplaces, extraKnownMarketplaces, enabledPlugins:
  https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugins/org
- managed-mcp.json, managedMcpServers, allowedMcpServers: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/managed-mcp
- Remote Control and the variables that switch it off, Trusted Devices: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/remote-control
- Which plugin parts load in chat, Cowork and Claude Code; organisation sync refuses bin/:
  https://claude.com/docs/plugins/org-rollout
- The .mobileconfig layout follows Apple's Configuration Profile Reference (com.apple.ManagedClient.preferences).

The sector templates point at open plugin catalogues the company's rules file can enable, each checked on
2026-10-02: anthropics/knowledge-work-plugins (Apache-2.0), anthropics/claude-for-legal (Apache-2.0),
anthropics/financial-services (Apache-2.0). Nothing from them is copied into firmcall.
